 2025, and on the middle value of the county&rsquo;s 6 grids September to October came in under 90% of normal in 35 of those 75 years, more than any other pair. In 2025, on the middle of the grids, November to December came in at 60% of normal and April to May at 139%. So far in 2026, March to April sits at 64% of normal on the middle of the grids. Every grid had its driest year in 2007, with grid 18786 at 63%.</p>"}
